\subsection{School Board Vote Roll Off}

Another dependent variable to look at is school board vote independent of turnout 
higher up the ticket. As we saw in Section \ref{subsec:undervote}, the extent 
of undervote is variable across districts across years. I explore whether 
any of the models above explain the difference between top ticket turnout and 
school board turnout. As much as undervote coincides with political relevance of
the school board race to the electorate, the relationships observed above should 
also be observed in the measure of undervote. 

Undervote has another advantage. As we saw in Section \ref{subsec:turnout}, turnout 
rose in 2011 due to the heightened interest in the state supreme court election 
between David Prosser and Joanne Kloppenburg. This makes it hard to attribute 
heightened school board voter turnout year to year to school boards when 
the turnout for the top ticket race changes year to year. The estimated difference in 
school board turnout to top ticket turnout can be one way to measure the political 
interest of voters in school boards. A disadvantage of this measure is that 
school board is not the only down-ticket race and undervote does not measure 
voter interest as many voters do not abstain. 

%CITATIONS

<<undervotetabs, results='asis'>>=
load("../../data/cache/springElectionVotes.rda")
# load("data/cache/springElectionVotes.rda")
springVotes$votesTopTicketSpring <- springVotes$VotesCast
springVotes$VotesCast <- NULL
dist_turn <- merge(dist_turn, springVotes, 
                   by = c("distid", "year"), all.x = TRUE)

dist_turn$topTicketTurnoutSpring <- dist_turn$votesTopTicketSpring / dist_turn$VAP_adj
dist_turn$turnoutDiff <- dist_turn$topTicketTurnoutSpring - dist_turn$turnout


moddat <- dist_turn[, c("turnout", "turnoutLag2", "turnoutDiff","year", 
                        "fallTurnout", "VAP_adjLOG", "distid", 
                        "per_white_all", "per65o", "PerBachelorOrAbove", "OOH_share", "median_incomeLOG", 
                        "CLOSE", "teachShareofVoters", "districtwide", "contest", 
                        "ImputedFlag")]
moddat$ImputedFlag[is.na(moddat$ImputedFlag)] <- "Observed"
moddat$ImputedFlag <- defac(moddat$ImputedFlag)
moddat$ImputedFlag[moddat$ImputedFlag == "Imputed2010"] <- "Imputed"
moddat$ImputedFlag[moddat$ImputedFlag == "Observed2010"] <- "Observed"
moddat$ImputedFlag <- factor(moddat$ImputedFlag, levels = c("Imputed", "Observed"))
moddat$ImputedFlag <- relevel(moddat$ImputedFlag, ref = "Imputed")

moddat <- na.omit(moddat)
moddat <- moddat[order(moddat$distid, moddat$year),]
moddat$distid <- factor(moddat$distid)
moddat$year <- factor(moddat$year)
moddat$districtwide <- factor(moddat$districtwide)
moddat$turnout <- moddat$turnout * 100
moddat$turnoutDiff <- moddat$turnoutDiff * 100
# moddat$turnoutLag2 <- moddat$turnoutLag2 * 100
# moddat$turnoutLag1 <- moddat$turnoutLag1 * 100
# moddat$per_white_all <- moddat$per_white_all * 100
# moddat$per65o <- moddat$per65o * 100
# moddat$PerBachelorOrAbove <- moddat$PerBachelorOrAbove * 100
# moddat$OOH_share <- moddat$OOH_share * 100
# moddat$fallTurnout <- moddat$fallTurnout * 100
# moddat$VAP_adj <- log(moddat$VAP_adj)
# moddat$median_income <- log(moddat$median_income)
centr <- mean(moddat$turnoutDiff)
stddev <- sd(moddat$turnoutDiff)
moddat$outflag <- (moddat$turnoutDiff - centr) / stddev
moddat <- moddat[moddat$outflag <= 5 & moddat$outflag >= -5,]

dd <<- datadist(moddat)
options(datadist="dd")

undvote1 <- lmer(turnoutDiff ~ turnoutLag2 * VAP_adjLOG + per_white_all + 
                   per65o + PerBachelorOrAbove + OOH_share + median_incomeLOG + CLOSE + 
                   contest + teachShareofVoters + (1|year) + (1|distid),
                   data = moddat)
undvote2 <- lmer(turnoutDiff ~ turnoutLag2 * VAP_adjLOG + per_white_all + 
                   per65o + PerBachelorOrAbove + OOH_share + median_incomeLOG + CLOSE + 
                   contest + teachShareofVoters + (1|distid),
                   data = moddat)

m0 <- lm(turnoutDiff ~ turnoutLag2 * VAP_adjLOG + per_white_all + 
                   per65o + PerBachelorOrAbove + OOH_share + median_incomeLOG + CLOSE + 
                   contest + teachShareofVoters , data = moddat) # fit the null model

## Add teacher interaction here as well

# REtest1 <- exactLRT(m = refitML(undvote2), m0 = m0)
# 
# # Test for year specific slopes
# m.slope <- update(undvote1, . ~ . - (1|year))
# m0 <- update(undvote1, . ~ . - (1|distid))
